  "meaning": "Bounds on the scaling discrepancy between scale_model's OpenSim-file route and OpenSim's ModelScaler, after removing the nominal conversion error. One factor s: (m_s - o_s) - s^k (m_n - o_n), which is zero for two exact similarities (k = 1 for lengths, moment arms and torque, 0 for normalized fibre length and force). Several factors: (m_s - m_n) - (o_s - o_n). They characterize the fixed synthetic pose grid, not biomechanical equivalence or clinical accuracy.",
  "justification": "Uniform bounds are about 1.5 times the measured maxima (OpenSim's moment-arm and muscle-equilibrium noise), with a 1 nm floor for positions, which agree to 4e-16 m. Anisotropic bounds are 8 to 16% above the measured maxima; the 0.357 mm position discrepancy is the documented child joint offset convention. Every bound rejects each mutation listed for it under covers (by at least 25%). No cross-model bound sees the mutations under regression_only, so the MyoSuite self-regression must reject them.",
